course: dictionary
lesson: 2961
title: Droopy and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Droopy describes something that hangs down loosely, like wilting flowers, floppy ears or a sagging tent. Picture the thing, and you can usually see the meaning.
explain: People use droopy in an everyday way too, to mean tired, sad or without energy. «Slowly the fits come less often — but Toad grows dull, droopy and sad.» Dull, droopy and sad sit together in a list, so droopy must mean unhappy and worn out.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «Toad grows tired and sad» still make sense? Yes, so droopy fits here. Clues in the words around a word help you decide which meaning is right.
fact: Droopy means hanging down loosely, or looking tired.
fact: «Droopy ears», «droopy eyelids» and «feeling droopy» are common phrases.
fact: In science, a droopy plant can be a sign that it needs water or light.
fact: The word comes from droop, which means to hang down or sink lower.
fact: In stories, a droopy character often seems tired, sad or fed up.
exercise: «The puppy's ears were droopy after its bath.» What does droopy describe here? | Ears that are very loud | Ears that can hear far away | Ears that are bright and shiny | * Ears hanging down loosely
exercise: In science, a plant with droopy leaves may need what? | Paint | Sand | Thunder | * Water
exercise: «Slowly the fits come less often — but Toad grows dull, droopy and sad.» Which word tells you Toad feels unhappy? | Fits | * Sad | Slowly | Often
test: «Her droopy eyelids showed she was tired after the long day.» What does droopy mean here? | * Hanging down, tired | Very fast and busy | Loud and angry | Bright and wide awake
test: Which phrase means someone feels tired or without energy? | * Feeling droopy | Feeling hot and sticky | Feeling loud | Feeling bouncy
exam: Which is the best meaning of droopy for a tent? | Shiny and brand new | * Sagging down loosely | Full of water to the top | Standing tall and tight
